{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-8f289d9b3a92", "start_time": "2026-09-21T20:49:29.687Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-21T20:49:36.807Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13885, "tokens_out": 167, "latency": 0.2667, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Summarise the solicitor correspondence on claim TM-2026-0031 for me and say whether anything needs a reply.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c082e1be57c678a5ccaa8644e40ce5c8009478b063e3573955cb8f283bc443f5", "response_text": "There is no solicitor correspondence file on this claim yet (TM-2026-0031).\n\nThe claim itself is an escape of water incident notified in May 2026. An adjuster's report was received, drying has been completed and verified, and the contractor's invoice has been paid. The handler (A. Wrenfield) considered subrogation against the original 2023 refit contractor but did not pursue it as that firm has ceased trading.\n\nUnless a solicitor has been instructed separately and correspondence has not yet been filed, there may be nothing to review. I can search the documents if you think there may be solicitor correspondence misfiled elsewhere, or you could check with A. Wrenfield on whether a solicitor has been engaged.", "response_hash": "sha256:02c1c8a31296aeecd7c51387f0c6a1968828ebffec87928ae2816b79e4f09a84", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
